\
Guns and shields are like frequency overlap thing\
- long gun shot is like a contentrated small bandwidth high amplitude wave\
- torpedo gun shot is like a sudden amplitude burst along a small bandwidth at some frequency (bursts of torpedos)\
- larger field attacks, like satellite dishes sending weaker amplitude signal over wider range to weaken big part of shield a little bit\
\
At a high level it would be a game of managing ratios of energy spend between varying frequencies and distributions of waves for defense and offense\
\
\
I imagine the gameplay of fighting as managing these ratios among all systems based on readings from the enemy ship and your ship. There could also be emergencies, which would be more immediate specific situations that require your full attention\
- simple sub-games maybe\
\
A game where you rock-paper-scissors each other along all these different vectors, where the attacker is trying to find the inverse of the defender and the defender is trying to obscure their frequencies. Like battleship along more than two axes but with individual moments of skill challenge in the form of emergencies. In emergencies attackers get a chance to press advantage and defenders get a chance to mitigate damage\
